<section>

# Business Context

Companies frequently treat every customer in the same way despite having customers with completely different purchasing behaviors.

Customer Segmentation allows organizations to identify homogeneous groups, enabling more personalized marketing campaigns, better customer experiences and more efficient allocation of commercial resources.

</section>

<section>

# Challenge

The dataset contained customers with different purchasing frequencies, spending patterns and behavioral characteristics.

The main challenges included:

- Cleaning inconsistent records.
- Scaling numerical features.
- Reducing dimensionality.
- Selecting an appropriate number of clusters.
- Interpreting clusters from a business perspective.

</section>

<section>

# Solution

An end-to-end clustering workflow was developed including:

- Data Cleaning
- Feature Engineering
- Feature Scaling
- Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
- K-Means Clustering
- Cluster Interpretation
- Business Recommendations

</section>

